WEBVTT

00:07.173 --> 00:09.467
[birds chirping]

00:48.089 --> 00:49.591
Easy, little guy.

00:49.674 --> 00:50.592
- [grunts]
- [bones crack]

00:51.384 --> 00:53.928
[birds cawing]

01:12.113 --> 01:13.740
What's he doing?

01:36.513 --> 01:37.847
You wanna live?

01:51.820 --> 01:53.029
[Arisu speaks softly]
I'm just…

01:54.572 --> 01:55.949
I wanna die in here.

01:58.827 --> 01:59.869
Yeah?

02:01.579 --> 02:02.622
I get it.

02:12.298 --> 02:14.300
[gloomy music]

02:16.302 --> 02:18.721
[fire crackling]

02:37.657 --> 02:39.367
[Usagi] Thank you for this meal.

02:41.119 --> 02:43.121
[gloomy music]

02:50.670 --> 02:52.797
[rain pattering]

03:12.942 --> 03:14.777
LIFE IN THE WOODS
BY HENRY DAVID THOREAU

03:18.656 --> 03:20.658
[gloomy music continues]

03:24.329 --> 03:26.789
[rain pattering]

03:53.024 --> 03:55.235
[theme music]

04:59.257 --> 05:00.591
[Usagi exhales deeply]

05:01.217 --> 05:02.844
It's so beautiful.

05:04.971 --> 05:06.222
[Shigenori] Yes.

05:08.725 --> 05:10.018
Dad…

05:12.770 --> 05:14.564
Let's say there really was a God.

05:15.481 --> 05:17.150
What would you ask for?

05:17.233 --> 05:18.693
[chuckles]

05:19.569 --> 05:20.903
Aah…

05:23.031 --> 05:24.240
Hmm…

05:27.702 --> 05:30.580
That there would be
more mountains for us to climb!

05:30.663 --> 05:33.041
Where no human being has ever been.

05:33.124 --> 05:34.042
Please, dear God!

05:34.625 --> 05:36.878
[both laugh]

05:38.087 --> 05:39.881
You're crazy.
[chuckles]

05:41.424 --> 05:45.762
Mountains like that don't exist
in the world today, Yuzuha.

05:47.305 --> 05:48.139
Your turn, now.

05:53.978 --> 05:56.481
I want this moment to last forever!

06:01.319 --> 06:02.528
[sighs]

06:03.529 --> 06:04.781
A mountaintop…

06:05.948 --> 06:07.158
is where I…

06:09.243 --> 06:12.163
A mountaintop is
where I can really be myself.

06:14.332 --> 06:16.793
Dad, you are the only one

06:17.376 --> 06:20.296
who makes me believe
that I have a place in this world.

06:24.175 --> 06:25.384
[sighs]

06:25.468 --> 06:27.845
I wanna live this moment forever.

06:32.350 --> 06:33.768
You'd get bored.

06:36.229 --> 06:38.898
[both laugh]

06:39.482 --> 06:43.402
[laughter echoes]

06:43.486 --> 06:46.072
[leaves rustling]

06:48.032 --> 06:49.367
[wind blowing]

06:49.450 --> 06:50.743
[reporter 1] That's his daughter!

06:50.827 --> 06:53.496
- [reporter 2] There she is!
- [reporter 3] Ms. Usagi! Ms. Usagi!

06:53.579 --> 06:55.832
[reporters clamoring]

06:55.915 --> 06:58.334
- I just wanna ask you…
- Did he actually climb Mount Everest?

06:58.417 --> 07:00.628
Is it true that your father didn't
actually make the climb

07:00.711 --> 07:01.546
that he said he did?

07:01.629 --> 07:04.006
Please… Ms. Usagi, Ms. Usagi, over here!

07:04.090 --> 07:06.134
[reporter 4] Please comment, please!

07:07.885 --> 07:09.011
[Shigenori] Welcome home.

07:12.348 --> 07:13.266
Dad.

07:14.851 --> 07:16.144
Don't you worry.

07:16.936 --> 07:18.980
I don't know who's spreading these lies,

07:19.897 --> 07:21.649
but I've always told you the truth.

07:29.323 --> 07:30.741
Where are you going?

07:31.742 --> 07:32.827
To the mountain.

07:36.456 --> 07:37.790
[door opens]

07:39.876 --> 07:41.961
[breathes nervously]

07:48.259 --> 07:49.343
Dad, wait.

07:49.427 --> 07:51.429
[soft music]

07:53.598 --> 07:54.682
[Shigenori] The mountain…

07:55.850 --> 07:58.186
is where I can really be myself.

08:10.573 --> 08:13.743
[reporters clamoring]

08:13.826 --> 08:14.869
[door closes]

08:23.586 --> 08:27.089
STAGED?

08:27.173 --> 08:30.092
SOLO NO-OXYGEN MOUNTAIN CLIMBING
SUSPECTED TO BE STAGED

08:30.176 --> 08:32.595
HE USED AN OXYGEN SUPPLEMENT

08:32.678 --> 08:35.598
IT WAS AN IMPOSSIBLE CHALLENGE
IN THE FIRST PLACE

08:35.681 --> 08:38.976
DID USAGI STAGE THE ENTIRE EVENT?

08:39.060 --> 08:42.104
550-STRONG SEARCH PARTY
LOOK FOR MISSING CLIMBER

08:42.188 --> 08:48.861
NO CLUES ON HIS WHEREABOUTS

08:48.945 --> 08:51.405
WORLD-FAMOUS MOUNTAINEER MISSING

08:51.489 --> 08:53.115
DID SHIGENORI USAGI
COMMIT SUICIDE

08:53.199 --> 08:55.117
DUE TO SUSPICIONS
ON STAGED MOUNTAIN CLIMBING?

08:55.201 --> 08:58.829
SUICIDE

09:06.212 --> 09:08.297
[dark music]

09:29.652 --> 09:31.445
[paper rustles]

10:02.018 --> 10:03.436
Thank you for the meal.

10:08.566 --> 10:10.735
[utensils clattering]

10:17.408 --> 10:18.784
[Arisu] Why did you save me?

10:23.664 --> 10:26.000
[stomach growls]

10:31.005 --> 10:33.382
Your body says, "I want to live."

10:36.135 --> 10:37.386
My body?

10:41.349 --> 10:43.225
Might say it wants to live…

10:44.143 --> 10:45.186
[scoffs]

10:47.063 --> 10:48.189
[inhales sharply]

10:49.732 --> 10:52.652
[shakily]
But I don't deserve to live anymore.

10:57.573 --> 10:59.116
They're all dead.

11:02.578 --> 11:04.914
And I'm the only one still alive.

11:08.250 --> 11:11.128
They all had to die so I could survive.

11:15.633 --> 11:18.260
I might as well have been the one
who killed them all.

11:18.844 --> 11:20.638
[Arisu sobs]

11:21.138 --> 11:23.349
[Arisu] I killed them all.

11:24.558 --> 11:25.851
[Arisu breathes shakily]

11:26.477 --> 11:28.979
I don't deserve to live.
[sniffs]

11:29.605 --> 11:32.066
Not after I let them all die.

11:35.111 --> 11:36.612
I have to die.

11:38.656 --> 11:39.990
I have to die.

11:41.409 --> 11:42.827
I have to die!

11:42.910 --> 11:44.703
[sobs]

11:45.204 --> 11:47.415
I have to die to be with them.

11:49.041 --> 11:53.587
I need to die!
I need to make it up to all of them!

11:54.713 --> 11:58.092
I need to make amends
for everything I've done!

12:01.387 --> 12:03.931
[Arisu whimpers]

12:07.893 --> 12:09.645
[Arisu sniffles]
Why?

12:12.523 --> 12:13.691
Why?

12:20.698 --> 12:21.699
I…

12:25.453 --> 12:26.787
I'm hungry.

12:33.461 --> 12:34.670
I understand.

12:35.754 --> 12:37.965
There was a time I wanted to die too.

12:43.387 --> 12:44.680
Just like you do.

12:47.308 --> 12:49.226
I was just laying on the ground.

12:50.936 --> 12:52.938
And I started feeling hungry.

12:59.403 --> 13:01.113
I know one day, I will die.

13:04.950 --> 13:07.786
And it could be
when we're playing the game tomorrow

13:08.454 --> 13:10.331
or when my visa expires.

13:17.588 --> 13:19.298
But for now, I made that food.

13:21.175 --> 13:22.968
So eat it while you're still alive.

13:25.846 --> 13:27.848
[soft music]

13:29.725 --> 13:30.768
[sighs]

13:53.123 --> 13:55.251
[gate scraping]

13:56.544 --> 13:58.546
[soft music continues]

13:59.964 --> 14:01.048
[Usagi grunts]

14:01.840 --> 14:03.926
[birds chirping in distance]

14:29.743 --> 14:33.038
[wings flapping]

14:34.748 --> 14:37.418
[Usagi panting]

14:50.556 --> 14:51.557
Get ready.

14:56.186 --> 14:57.897
[Usagi] You've got a game to play.

15:01.275 --> 15:02.359
[sighs]

15:03.402 --> 15:05.571
Are you planning to die
by having your visa expire?

15:06.238 --> 15:08.365
[water sloshing]

15:18.500 --> 15:20.336
That time you screamed at all of us.

15:26.467 --> 15:27.301
[Usagi sighs]

15:27.384 --> 15:28.928
[Usagi] During the tag game…

15:32.348 --> 15:34.808
You risked your life
trying to save everyone.

15:35.935 --> 15:37.061
- Everyone!
- [Karube] Hey!

15:37.144 --> 15:39.772
He's up here! Over here,
he's on the second level!

15:39.855 --> 15:42.024
Tell us where he is if you see him!

15:42.107 --> 15:44.026
And let's all look for the symbol!

15:49.281 --> 15:50.950
I didn't wanna die then.

15:57.206 --> 15:59.291
[Arisu]
And I didn't want anyone else too, either.

16:04.213 --> 16:05.631
I know what you're saying.

16:07.424 --> 16:09.343
And I don't want you to die now.

16:12.930 --> 16:16.433
If you hadn't screamed back there,
I'd be dead now.

16:17.601 --> 16:19.603
[emotional music]

16:27.444 --> 16:28.821
Let me repay you.

16:37.079 --> 16:39.415
[uplifting music]

17:00.436 --> 17:02.896
[intense music]

17:06.775 --> 17:08.902
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

17:08.986 --> 17:10.237
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

17:10.320 --> 17:13.907
THE GAME ARENA IS UP AHEAD

17:13.991 --> 17:16.326
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

17:28.005 --> 17:30.007
[intense music continues]

17:56.617 --> 17:58.994
[tense music]

18:53.841 --> 18:55.384
1 PER PERSON

19:06.270 --> 19:09.064
FACE RECOGNITION IN PROGRESS
PLEASE WAIT FOR A MOMENT

19:10.524 --> 19:12.067
You're not newbies.

19:14.736 --> 19:15.988
And who are you?

19:17.281 --> 19:19.366
We're the guys
who cleared four games together.

19:20.325 --> 19:23.829
We met at the first game
and now we work together as a team.

19:24.955 --> 19:28.458
But we might need more
if we're gonna clear this one.

19:31.211 --> 19:33.130
And your leg? Are you hurt?

19:35.757 --> 19:38.927
Ah… I tweaked it a bit.

19:40.262 --> 19:41.430
In the game?

19:44.558 --> 19:45.642
Yeah.

19:49.271 --> 19:50.480
[phones chiming]

19:50.564 --> 19:52.232
[Yamane] Okay, the game's starting.

19:52.316 --> 19:54.693
[announcer] Registration is now closed.

19:54.776 --> 19:57.070
The game is about to commence.

19:57.154 --> 19:59.406
Difficulty, Four of Clubs.

19:59.489 --> 20:02.659
There are a total of five participants.

20:02.743 --> 20:04.369
Game, "Distance".

20:04.453 --> 20:06.371
"Distance"?

20:06.955 --> 20:11.251
[announcer] Rule. Endure the trial
while striving for the goal 

20:11.335 --> 20:12.836
within the time limit.

20:13.670 --> 20:14.755
Clear condition.

20:15.339 --> 20:17.424
Safely attain the goal.

20:18.008 --> 20:19.176
What is this?

20:19.676 --> 20:21.428
[announcer] The game will now commence.

20:22.012 --> 20:24.890
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] 120 minutes remaining.

20:26.141 --> 20:27.226
[sighs]

20:27.935 --> 20:29.728
[Takuma] Does this mean we have to run?

20:30.979 --> 20:32.356
What do you think, Seizan?

20:32.439 --> 20:34.483
[clock ticking]

20:35.359 --> 20:36.485
[Seizan] "Distance"?

20:37.736 --> 20:38.862
Zero.

20:38.946 --> 20:40.989
[ominous music]

20:41.740 --> 20:44.201
[Arisu] We have to run? On the highway?

20:46.495 --> 20:48.247
Uh, run?
[groans]

20:48.330 --> 20:50.540
[Yamane] Takuma. Just relax.

20:50.624 --> 20:51.750
[Takuma grunts]

20:51.833 --> 20:53.168
[Seizan] Sit down, sit down.

20:53.961 --> 20:56.880
[Yamane] I think these old buses
from the '70s all have V8 engines.

20:56.964 --> 20:58.048
[clattering]

20:59.174 --> 21:00.008
- [keys jingle]
- [Yamane grunts]

21:00.092 --> 21:01.969
- [Yamane] Let's hope it starts.
- [engine splutters]

21:02.052 --> 21:04.096
- [Yamane] Come on, baby!
- [engine splutters]

21:04.179 --> 21:06.723
[engine splutters]

21:06.807 --> 21:08.141
[grunts]

21:08.225 --> 21:09.935
[Yamane] Shit! It's out of gas.

21:11.478 --> 21:13.188
Looks like we have to run.

21:19.611 --> 21:20.821
Go on. Leave me here.

21:21.321 --> 21:23.657
[suspenseful music]

21:28.662 --> 21:30.706
- Takuma!
- [Takuma] Listen to me.

21:31.581 --> 21:34.751
I don't plan to just sit on my ass here,
roll over, and die.

21:36.920 --> 21:39.089
I'm gonna try to find a way to survive.

21:40.841 --> 21:42.134
But you gotta go.

21:46.471 --> 21:48.974
- We're not leaving you behind!
- [Takuma] Yamane!

21:51.143 --> 21:53.353
[shouts]
You gotta survive, so go now!

21:54.563 --> 21:56.356
You wanna see your wife again, right?

21:57.399 --> 21:59.818
[Takuma]
And what about that baby she's carrying?

22:02.029 --> 22:04.573
What the hell are they supposed to do
without you?

22:04.656 --> 22:06.241
[breathes heavily]

22:06.325 --> 22:08.535
[somber music]

22:11.413 --> 22:14.458
Don't worry about me. I got this.

22:23.467 --> 22:24.551
Yamane.

22:26.428 --> 22:27.679
Let's go.

22:32.893 --> 22:33.935
[Takuma] Go on.

22:35.896 --> 22:36.772
Now.

22:37.689 --> 22:38.857
You can do this.

22:40.192 --> 22:42.402
[somber music continues]

22:48.700 --> 22:49.951
[Seizan] Let's go.

22:58.585 --> 22:59.669
Let's go.

23:10.222 --> 23:11.890
[Usagi] He made the right choice.

23:21.149 --> 23:22.317
[phone chiming]

23:22.400 --> 23:25.112
[announcer] 110 minutes remaining.

23:30.909 --> 23:32.953
[tense music]

23:40.001 --> 23:40.919
[Usagi exhales sharply]

23:50.887 --> 23:52.055
Arisu.

23:52.139 --> 23:53.306
Live for us.

23:53.890 --> 23:55.142
Thank you.

23:55.225 --> 23:57.519
[suspenseful music]

24:17.706 --> 24:19.249
[all panting]

24:22.210 --> 24:23.378
[phone chimes]

24:23.461 --> 24:25.255
[announcer] Distance, 1,000.

24:25.755 --> 24:27.632
[Usagi panting]

24:34.681 --> 24:37.809
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] 90 minutes remaining.

24:39.227 --> 24:40.520
[Arisu] To reach the goal,

24:41.438 --> 24:43.398
how much further do we have to run?

24:43.481 --> 24:45.650
[panting]

24:51.907 --> 24:54.409
[breathing heavily]

24:55.410 --> 24:58.830
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 5,000.

25:00.081 --> 25:03.043
[all panting]

25:05.629 --> 25:06.588
Hey.

25:07.380 --> 25:08.590
What's that?

25:14.971 --> 25:16.890
REPLENISHMENT STATION

25:16.973 --> 25:19.684
[all panting]

25:22.312 --> 25:23.605
[Seizan] We made it.

25:31.696 --> 25:32.572
Wait.

25:32.656 --> 25:34.491
- Hang on a sec.
- Eh?

25:37.494 --> 25:39.246
You're waiting for us to drink it,
aren't you?

25:42.624 --> 25:43.917
No, we're not.

25:52.342 --> 25:53.510
[Usagi] Drink this.

25:54.719 --> 25:55.637
Thank you.

26:00.892 --> 26:02.102
[gulping]

26:04.938 --> 26:05.981
[coughs]

26:07.816 --> 26:08.984
That was great.

26:11.820 --> 26:13.947
[all breathing heavily]

26:17.492 --> 26:18.743
Are you sure?

26:19.619 --> 26:20.620
Uh-huh.

26:25.667 --> 26:26.918
[sighs]

26:28.503 --> 26:29.504
[Seizan coughs]

26:37.137 --> 26:38.763
[all panting]

26:38.847 --> 26:41.766
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 6,000.

26:43.768 --> 26:46.271
[Yamane] Man, it's dark in here.

26:53.570 --> 26:57.699
[Arisu] Shit, this isn't Clubs.
It's gotta be a game of Spades.

26:57.782 --> 26:59.993
[all panting]

27:01.328 --> 27:02.912
[Usagi] Something's over there.

27:10.879 --> 27:12.255
[Yamane] I don't see anything.

27:12.839 --> 27:14.841
Yeah. Right there.

27:20.096 --> 27:22.599
[approaching footsteps]

27:23.516 --> 27:25.518
[ominous music]

27:27.395 --> 27:28.980
[ominous music intensifies]

27:29.064 --> 27:30.315
[gasps]

27:31.941 --> 27:33.360
[all yell]

27:33.443 --> 27:34.527
[Usagi] Run!

27:34.611 --> 27:35.945
[roars]

27:36.613 --> 27:38.365
[all panting]

27:40.367 --> 27:41.701
[growls]

27:42.702 --> 27:46.498
[panther growling]

27:48.875 --> 27:50.960
- [roars]
- [Yamane grunts]

27:57.634 --> 27:59.135
[roars]

28:00.261 --> 28:02.430
[breathes heavily]

28:08.728 --> 28:11.231
[both panting]

28:18.988 --> 28:21.032
- [thuds]
- [panther growls]

28:21.116 --> 28:23.201
[grunts]

28:23.785 --> 28:25.412
[panther growling]

28:29.999 --> 28:32.752
[breathing shakily]

28:35.130 --> 28:37.048
- [roars]
- [Arisu screams]

28:37.132 --> 28:38.842
[action music]

28:38.925 --> 28:40.802
[panting]

28:41.511 --> 28:43.054
- [growls]
- [squeaks]

28:43.638 --> 28:45.849
[panther growls]

28:51.980 --> 28:53.773
[grunts]

28:53.857 --> 28:55.358
- [roars]
- [grunts]

28:58.069 --> 28:58.945
[yells]

28:59.028 --> 29:00.989
[growling]

29:05.118 --> 29:07.203
[action music continues]

29:10.331 --> 29:11.416
[hissing]

29:14.836 --> 29:15.962
[Arisu screams]

29:18.923 --> 29:20.759
[panting]

29:25.096 --> 29:28.516
Oh my god, oh my god. Help me!

29:29.642 --> 29:31.102
- [panther roars]
- [Seizan screams]

29:31.186 --> 29:34.314
- [flesh tearing]
- [Seizan screaming]

29:34.397 --> 29:36.107
[yelling]

29:36.733 --> 29:37.984
Help!

29:39.068 --> 29:42.113
No! Get off!
[screaming]

29:42.197 --> 29:43.281
Seizan!

29:43.364 --> 29:44.824
- [Usagi] Let's go!
- Come on!

29:44.908 --> 29:45.742
Get off!

29:45.825 --> 29:48.578
[screams]

29:48.661 --> 29:51.122
Seizan! Seizan!

29:52.499 --> 29:55.418
[all panting]

29:56.044 --> 29:58.546
- [Yamane] I can't run anymore.
- Come on!

30:02.300 --> 30:03.384
I'm done.

30:06.805 --> 30:07.806
I can't.

30:07.889 --> 30:09.724
[breathes heavily]

30:10.517 --> 30:13.436
[both panting]

30:14.020 --> 30:15.480
I'd only been with them…

30:16.773 --> 30:18.316
for about a week, but…

30:21.361 --> 30:23.029
it's like I knew them both…

30:24.447 --> 30:26.199
for my entire life.

30:34.916 --> 30:36.292
You gotta live.

30:36.960 --> 30:38.795
So you can tell your wife about them.

30:49.681 --> 30:50.682
You're right.

31:03.736 --> 31:06.906
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 8,000.

31:06.990 --> 31:08.741
[all panting]

31:21.963 --> 31:23.047
What are you doing?

31:24.048 --> 31:25.091
A motorcycle.

31:27.719 --> 31:29.345
[Arisu] Royal Enfield.

31:31.472 --> 31:32.724
[Yamane] You know bikes?

31:34.350 --> 31:36.185
Diesel engines like that are pretty rare.

31:40.857 --> 31:43.151
But old stuff like this still works

31:43.234 --> 31:46.154
since none of it has any IC chips.

31:48.656 --> 31:49.657
Hang on.

31:50.450 --> 31:51.910
Electronics.

31:53.036 --> 31:55.830
All electrical circuits
have been destroyed.

31:56.915 --> 31:57.749
So?

31:57.832 --> 32:01.002
Analog stuff
with no electrical circuitry still works.

32:01.085 --> 32:03.338
All motorcycles and all the cars
still work.

32:03.421 --> 32:06.341
Like this bike, or that bus back there!

32:08.301 --> 32:10.428
[Arisu grunts]

32:11.054 --> 32:12.764
Damn it, no battery.

32:13.973 --> 32:15.058
[liquid sloshing]

32:15.141 --> 32:18.019
This bike, you said it's got
an old diesel engine, right?

32:18.102 --> 32:19.145
Uh-huh.

32:19.228 --> 32:21.606
So it doesn't run on regular gas,
but diesel.

32:22.190 --> 32:24.275
- So does the bus, nice!
- [Arisu] Uh-huh.

32:25.693 --> 32:27.528
[Usagi sighs]
Wait, so…

32:27.612 --> 32:30.198
You want to carry that bike
all the way back with you?

32:30.281 --> 32:33.868
If we get this fuel back there,
we can use the bus and save Takuma.

32:33.952 --> 32:35.662
You wanna save Takuma?

32:35.745 --> 32:37.413
- [Arisu] Uh-huh.
- But if we go back,

32:37.497 --> 32:39.248
then the game can't be cleared!

32:39.332 --> 32:41.709
Yes it can. There's still enough time.

32:42.460 --> 32:44.712
But just in case, you two keep going.

32:44.796 --> 32:47.590
If I can start that bus,
I'll catch up real fast.

32:48.883 --> 32:51.177
No more surviving
by letting other people die.

32:52.178 --> 32:53.221
I'm done with it.

32:58.851 --> 33:01.479
[Arisu panting]

33:07.527 --> 33:09.737
[foreboding music]

33:13.533 --> 33:16.953
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 7,000.

33:17.537 --> 33:20.373
[both panting]

33:22.250 --> 33:25.503
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 10,000.

33:36.639 --> 33:39.058
[announcer] Distance, 6,000.

33:39.809 --> 33:43.396
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 12,000.

33:48.484 --> 33:52.030
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 4,000.

33:52.113 --> 33:53.990
[panting]

33:55.783 --> 33:58.119
[intense music]

34:05.251 --> 34:06.210
What?

34:08.546 --> 34:09.589
[Yamane] That's the goal.

34:10.256 --> 34:12.133
[both breathing heavily]

34:12.967 --> 34:15.428
All right, let's wait for them.

34:17.263 --> 34:19.640
[intense music continues]

34:21.976 --> 34:23.436
[grunts]

34:23.519 --> 34:26.731
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Distance, 1,000.

34:31.152 --> 34:34.822
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] 15 minutes remaining.

34:37.241 --> 34:38.534
[Arisu] Hey!

34:46.793 --> 34:48.086
Hey!

34:49.253 --> 34:51.756
[intense music continues]

34:57.011 --> 34:58.387
Hey!

35:02.266 --> 35:04.811
[panting heavily]

35:11.943 --> 35:15.655
ENTRY PROHIBITED

35:24.038 --> 35:25.164
[Usagi] Your wife?

35:32.380 --> 35:35.049
This autumn, we're expecting a baby.

35:45.810 --> 35:47.979
I'm sure
they're waiting for you somewhere.

35:53.776 --> 35:54.902
Somewhere…

35:57.280 --> 35:58.406
they're waiting.

36:01.784 --> 36:03.619
[sighs]
Everyone's waiting.

36:05.204 --> 36:07.248
[sentimental music]

36:08.624 --> 36:10.501
They're all out there somewhere.

36:18.676 --> 36:20.678
So you have to stay alive to see them.

36:33.107 --> 36:35.985
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Five minutes remaining.

36:36.527 --> 36:38.070
Doesn't look like they made it.

36:39.488 --> 36:40.364
[sighs]

36:41.782 --> 36:44.160
- [ricochets]
- [metal clattering]

36:44.243 --> 36:45.286
[both gasp]

36:45.369 --> 36:46.787
What the hell was that?

36:47.371 --> 36:49.415
- [ricochet]
- [clattering]

36:50.416 --> 36:51.417
[rumbling]

36:51.500 --> 36:53.002
What is that?

36:53.085 --> 36:55.087
[rumbling in distance]

37:00.718 --> 37:02.053
[rattling]

37:02.720 --> 37:03.638
Water?

37:04.889 --> 37:06.807
[rumbling continues]

37:08.768 --> 37:09.685
- [clanks]
- [water hissing]

37:11.520 --> 37:12.772
[clangs]

37:13.439 --> 37:15.066
[both gasp]

37:15.650 --> 37:18.319
- [rumbling continues]
- [water hissing]

37:18.402 --> 37:21.239
[both panting]

37:21.948 --> 37:24.200
[metal groaning intensifies]

37:30.373 --> 37:32.583
[rumbles]

37:33.209 --> 37:35.044
[explodes]

37:35.127 --> 37:39.131
[tense music]

37:39.215 --> 37:42.510
[rumbling, crashing]

37:43.344 --> 37:45.221
[both panting]

37:45.805 --> 37:48.391
[rumbling continues]

37:51.936 --> 37:53.104
[Yamane grunts]

37:54.981 --> 37:56.190
I can't run anymore!

37:56.274 --> 37:58.776
[shouts]
Yes, you can! Don't look back!

38:01.821 --> 38:02.780
[Yamane] Ah!

38:04.532 --> 38:05.866
[pants]

38:10.037 --> 38:11.205
[screams]

38:13.791 --> 38:16.043
[pants heavily]

38:22.258 --> 38:25.177
[horn honking]

38:27.722 --> 38:28.806
[shouts]
Usagi!

38:30.683 --> 38:31.809
[whimpering]

38:32.727 --> 38:33.561
[gasps]

38:33.644 --> 38:35.688
[tense music continues]

38:36.272 --> 38:37.356
[shouts]
Arisu!

38:44.739 --> 38:46.949
- [grunts]
- [tires screeching]

38:47.033 --> 38:48.284
[screams]

38:51.620 --> 38:54.498
[crashing, rumbling]

39:04.300 --> 39:05.301
[water splatters]

39:13.517 --> 39:16.187
[water splattering]

39:24.695 --> 39:26.614
[grunts]
Arisu.

39:28.032 --> 39:28.991
[groans]

39:33.788 --> 39:35.790
[breathes deeply]

39:39.210 --> 39:40.503
[groans]

39:45.925 --> 39:48.511
[Arisu grunts]

39:49.678 --> 39:50.930
[Usagi] Oh, it hurts.

39:54.475 --> 39:55.768
Are you all right?

40:02.483 --> 40:05.152
[grunting]

40:10.825 --> 40:12.743
[Takuma] Thank you. Thanks.

40:23.921 --> 40:26.340
[suspenseful music]

40:34.390 --> 40:35.683
Goal.

40:37.893 --> 40:39.562
So this whole time…

40:41.647 --> 40:43.274
I was at the goal?

40:46.819 --> 40:49.488
[Takuma] It was right there for us to see.

40:49.572 --> 40:52.450
The bus was the goal from the very start.

40:53.617 --> 40:56.287
Then what were all those numbers about?

40:56.370 --> 40:57.913
The distance to the goal.

40:59.331 --> 41:00.875
[Arisu] We were safe at zero.

41:04.712 --> 41:06.130
[phones chiming]

41:09.884 --> 41:11.469
[announcer] Game cleared.

41:11.552 --> 41:13.846
Congratulations.

41:16.098 --> 41:17.641
[both grunt]

41:19.185 --> 41:20.394
[Arisu] I got you.

41:30.529 --> 41:31.447
[Usagi grunts]

41:34.575 --> 41:36.452
Hey, wait! Where are you going?

41:43.292 --> 41:44.460
I, uh…

41:46.462 --> 41:47.796
I have no idea.

41:56.096 --> 41:57.598
But I hope that…

42:01.477 --> 42:03.187
we'll meet again.

42:16.325 --> 42:18.452
[solemn music]

42:33.634 --> 42:35.010
[Usagi] The Beach?

42:36.136 --> 42:38.847
[Arisu] Maybe the people
who disappeared are there.

42:38.931 --> 42:41.850
[Usagi] Could it be
some kind of evacuation shelter?

42:42.476 --> 42:43.852
[Arisu] Yeah, maybe.

42:45.229 --> 42:47.022
But there's an answer out there.

42:49.483 --> 42:51.694
And I wanna remember Karube's words.

42:54.029 --> 42:55.573
I'm gonna do it for everyone.

42:57.241 --> 42:59.785
I'm gonna find the mastermind
of this sick game.

43:00.869 --> 43:02.913
And get this world back to the way it was.

43:05.457 --> 43:06.542
I swear it.

43:10.462 --> 43:14.174
But to do that,
I have to head to the Beach.

43:17.386 --> 43:19.805
[grandiose music]

43:40.534 --> 43:42.369
You really don't know how to ride a bike?

43:43.203 --> 43:44.455
I never learned how.

43:45.080 --> 43:46.874
That's pretty hard to believe.

43:51.295 --> 43:53.297
[Usagi] But this feels nice.

43:53.380 --> 43:56.717
[grandiose music continues]

44:11.774 --> 44:14.109
[closing theme music]
